                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This does not constitute \"Minimum Sellable Product\".\n\nThere are a grand total of perhaps 8 rooms. Of those, One is a plot room, three introduce new concepts, three test your understanding of those concepts, and finally there's one room with an interesting scenario which lasts all of 15 seconds before the game abruptly ends.\n\nI've dabbled in indie game development, and this quantity of gameplay is something I'd post on a gamedev forum going \"Hey guys, I got the engine going!\", not something I'd be going \"Hey guys! I'm ready to sell my first game!\"\n\nThere are some really interesting ideas in this short game. I'd like to see the tools given used in a few more ways. There's an opportunity for this to be a cool sort of action/puzzle game where you use your psychic powers to deal with increasingly complex scenarios. It doesn't have to be a 40 hour game, but as it stands, this isn't Minimum Sellable Product. It's a tutorial and the first level.",
